"""
Virtual Machine: bytecode interpreter loop.

Executes CompiledFunction bytecode produced by the compiler
(bytecode/compiler.na.jac). Each JS function call pushes a CallFrame; the frame owns
the local-variable slots, the catch-handler IP stack, and the captured free-variable
list for closures. All frames share one operand stack (see VM below).

ECMAScript spec : §9 — Executable Code and Execution Contexts
                  https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-executable-code-and-execution-contexts
"""

